  "boxes": [
    {
      "type": "anchorbox",
      "title": "The Scholar and the Protector",
      "description": "He holds a devastating weapon (Bajra) in his hand, but wears the sacred thread (Janeu) of a peaceful scholar on his shoulder. This is the ultimate balance we should all strive for: possessing a highly educated, peaceful mind, while remaining strong enough to fiercely protect others from injustice.",
      "motivating_text": "",
      "citation": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "gotchabox",
      "items": [
        "Nasalization: Pay close attention to the चन्द्रबिन्दु (Chandrabindu / Moon-dot) on काँधे (Kaandhe) and मूँज (Moonja). This nasalizes the vowel without adding the extra weight of a full consonant, preserving the 16-beat meter.",
        "Conjunct Consonant Weight (बज्र): The `a` in `ba` becomes a 2-beat Guru because it precedes the conjunct `jra`!"
      ]
    }
  ]
